EXTRAS={
'garden': 'A low container beside the path holds labels from earlier plantings. She checks which names are still readable before making replacements. One plant has begun to lean toward a gap in the fence, and she compares its stem with the position drawn in the notebook. The other gardener moves a small stool closer so that both can look at the leaves without stepping into the bed. A few insects move beneath a leaf as it is lifted gently.',
'clouds': 'A line of taller trees marks the edge of a nearby road. Their shadows move across a patch of bare ground at a different speed from the cloud shadows. The observer watches the two patterns overlap and then separate. Farther away, a darker band of cloud has begun to hide part of a hill. The changing view gives another opportunity to compare the direction of the wind at different heights. The observer records the time beside a sketch of the cloud outline.',
'station_story': 'The bicycle owner returned from the ticket office with a leaflet folded over one hand. He checked the position of the carriage symbols on the platform sign and moved a little farther along the fence. The child pointed toward the first visible window of the train. Her grandfather lifted the paper bag from the bench and asked her to stand beside him. Nora took one step back to leave a clear route for anyone getting off. She could now see the reflection of the station roof in the approaching windows.',
'bicycle': 'A small bag beneath the saddle contains the items normally carried for minor problems on the route. The rider checks that it is fastened securely and that nothing hangs near the wheel. A water bottle fits into a holder on the frame without pressing against a moving part. The rider rolls the bicycle a short distance and listens once more while turning the handlebars gently. This gives another view of the cables and the space available around the front wheel.',
'pottery': 'The smaller tool leaves a narrow line that is easier to control near the base. She examines the line in the window light before making a second movement. The other worker holds the tray steady and moves one unused tool farther from the edge. A little water has gathered in the cloth, so the potter folds a dry part beneath the bowl. She compares the supported edge with the sketch in her notebook and checks how the curve meets the flat base.',
'library': 'One returned volume has a paper slip tucked between two pages. The worker removes the slip and puts it in a small container kept for loose materials. He checks the pages on either side before returning the book to the sorting tray. The librarian brings another map from the cabinet so the visitor can compare the scale. A clear label on its cover identifies the area shown. The visitor moves a chair closer to inspect the symbols beside the river.',
'laundry': 'A folded sheet rests on the upper part of the rack and shades a smaller item below it. The person moves the sheet to leave more space around that item. A thick seam still feels cool and damp even though the nearby fabric feels dry. The person compares the seam with the label instructions and checks that the rack remains stable after the garments have been rearranged. A slight movement of air can be felt near the open doorway.',
'map': 'The companion notices a narrow line continuing beyond the printed name of the bridge. They check the legend to see whether it represents a path or a boundary. A small bend in the river appears in both the map and the view from the crossing. The walker uses that match to reconsider the position of the two paths. The paper is folded back carefully so that the relevant section remains visible as they prepare to examine the next sign.',
'echo': 'The listener then stands nearer a curtain while the speaker remains in the same place. A pencil mark on the drawing records this new position. The sentence is repeated at a similar volume, leaving time for the sound to fade before anyone speaks again. The people compare what they heard without assuming that a louder impression means a longer echo. A row of empty chairs stands between them and one wall, adding another detail to the arrangement they are examining.',
'bread': 'A light cover protects the resting dough without pressing against its surface. The baker lifts one corner briefly to inspect the outline and then puts it back. A narrow strip of flour marks the place where the piece was shaped. The baker checks the prepared tray and compares its size with the space available in the oven. Another bowl contains a smaller mixture being rested for a different part of the work. Its surface looks less smooth than the first.',
'market_story': 'His sister chose a smaller bunch and asked the seller to place it beside the basket while she checked the list. Daniel looked toward a stand where several jars were arranged in rows. The labels faced the street, but he moved closer to read the smaller writing. Behind the stand, a person was adding fresh jars to an empty space on the table. His sister joined him with the vegetables, and they discussed which items would fit comfortably in their bag.',
'river': 'A narrow stick caught against the reeds moves slightly whenever a small wave reaches it. The observer compares its movement with that of a leaf farther from the bank. The worker steadies the measuring pole and waits for the surface to settle enough to read the mark. On the opposite side, a patch of exposed soil shows the outline of an older water level. The observer adds that shape to the sketch and checks its position against the nearby stones.'}
